            <ArticleTitle>Coronary artery bypass surgery or drug eluting stent for unprotected left main coronary artery disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>287-91</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary artery bypass surgery (CABG) is the treatment of choice in unprotected left main coronary artery disease (ULMCA). However drug eluting stent (DES) implantations in ULMCA have ushered a revolution in the field of percutaneous coronary interventions (PCI) for left main coronary artery (LMCA) by reducing peri-procedural mortality and incidence of major adverse cardiac events (MACE). More randomized trials and follow-up studies are required before PCI with DES can be chosen as alternative to CABG.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
